    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "51dd29c9cceb478891c17fee69ceb7af",
    "m_Title": "Bubble Advection",
    "m_Content": "This subgraph adds a small amount of animation. We sample the 3D noise twice at irrational scales and multiply them together. We then use this unique value to slightly push the advection vector towards the surface normal. By varying how much the shift is by the two samples we just took, we can break up the surface of the liquid a little bit by pushing the voronoi samples into slightly different planes on Y. Because this effect is hard to track when combined with the others, this always uses the baked noise rather than having a procedural option. ",
